Aypa Power, a Blackstone portfolio company, is a leading developer, owner, and operator of utility-scale energy storage and hybrid renewable projects that power our communities and cities. Our mission is to responsibly decarbonize the grid and make North American energy markets more affordable, sustainable, and efficient. Aypa is well-capitalized and uniquely positioned to lean forward on projects with well-suited deal structures to meet our customers' needs. We have been at the forefront of energy storage development since our first energy storage project came online in 2018. As a leader in our industry, we have over 22 GW of utility-scale energy storage and hybrid renewable energy projects in development and 33 projects in operation or construction across North America.


We are seeking a Procurement Manager to support our work as a utility-scale energy storage and renewables leader. You will be responsible for supporting the development, growth, and execution of Aypa's renewables procurement platform of energy storage, solar hybrid technologies. This position will include direct interfacing with vendors, informed market analytics, and contracting support. This role is core to fostering Aypa's growth with targeted and informed investment in the right equipment, suppliers, service providers, and legal counsel. In this role, you will drive procurement strategies, negotiate complex supply and long-term service agreements, and maintain strategic vendor relationships while ensuring we achieve our economic targets, quality standards, and project timelines.


The right candidate needs to be comfortable learning and adapting with an evolving industry, working in a fast-paced entrepreneurial environment, nurturing relationships with providers, performing contracting, and collaborating with internal and external teams across the organization and industry. Success requires balancing competitive sourcing pressures with relationship building, technical problem solving with commercial rigor, and addressing immediate project needs with long-term strategic considerations.


**Responsibilities:**



* Strategic Sourcing:

+ Lead all sourcing activities for BESS and solar equipment, including market assessment, RFP development, vendor evaluation, and contract execution;
+ Develop and implement sourcing strategies that optimize price competitiveness, technical specifications, delivery reliability, supplier stability, and risk mitigation;
+ Manage comprehensive equipment supply agreements encompassing scope, commercial and payment terms, logistics, quality standards, and warranty provisions;

* Vendor Management & Networking:

+ Actively build, maintain, and prioritize key vendor and contractor relationships, including regular meetings to be a subject matter expert for Aypa on each of these supply segments and vendor status;
+ Serve as the primary point of contact and subject matter expert and ensure vendor alignment with company objectives;

* Negotiation and Deal Execution:

+ Lead negotiations on complex commercial and technical terms; identify creative solutions to overcome obstacles and drive deals to closure;

* Cross team Collaboration:

+ Partner closely with Engineering, Construction, Legal, and Development to ensure requirements are captured within Supply contracts and recommendations;
+ Work closely with internal and external resources to structure, negotiate, and close project transactions;

* Process Improvement

+ Champion procurement efficiency initiatives that enhance operational scalability, reduce costs, and strengthen supply chain resilience;
+ Continuously evaluate and recommend process improvements to support company growth;

* Transaction Support:

+ Work closely with internal and external resources to structure, negotiate and close project transactions related to acquisitions, financings, and divestitures, as well as commercial and technical contract agreements;

* General

+ Provide procurement insights and recommendations to inform company business plans, development strategy, and long-term supply chain positioning;

* Other duties as required or assigned.

**Key Qualifications:**

* Minimum of five (5) years of Procurement experience with progressive responsibility in sourcing, contract negotiation, and vendor management;
* Minimum of three (3) years of Procurement experience in utility-scale renewables, high-voltage procurement, and/or thermal procurement;
* Bachelor's degree in Engineering, Business, Finance, Supply Chain Management, or related field;
* Strong technical foundation: ability to understand equipment specifications, performance requirements, and technical trade-offs. Can confidently lead and engage in technical discussions with suppliers and internal stakeholders;
* Experience in supporting the successful execution of EPC and supply contracts;
* Solid understanding of utility-scale renewable energy project development, U.S power markets, transmission interconnection, a

**Pardgroup**
, a leading company in integrated services for retail and large-scale distribution, is looking for a new
**Procurement Manager**
to join our Team in New York.

The new colleague will carry out the following activities:

* Executing category management strategies to optimize Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) and expand a resilient supplier base through proactive global and domestic sourcing;
* Identifying, evaluating, and qualifying new suppliers to strengthen supply continuity, while maintaining strong Executing category management strategies to optimize Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) and expand a resilient supplier base through proactive global and domestic sourcing;
* Identifying, evaluating, and qualifying new suppliers to strengthen supply continuity, while maintaining strong relationships with key vendors to reduce risks and enhance competitive advantage;
* Leading formal Requests for Information, Proposals, and Quotations processes, while negotiating pricing and contractual terms to secure best-in-class agreements;
* Drafting, reviewing, and managing comprehensive procurement contracts in alignment with business objectives;
* Developing and maintaining strong relationships with key vendors, negotiating favorable rates, terms, and agreements;
* Regularly monitoring costs related to procurement activities;
* Collaborating with Quality Assurance and Engineering teams to resolve supplier quality and delivery issues using preventive and corrective action methodologies;
* Overseeing Procure-to-Pay activities, monitoring budgets, reporting savings and compliance metrics, and ensuring strict adherence to procurement policies, ethical standards, and regulatory requirements;
* Continuously assessing vendor performance and implementing improvement strategies.

The ideal candidate will meet the following requirements:

* Previous work experience in a similar role of at least 5 years, ideally within Interior Fit-out or Luxury industries; experience with materials such as metal, glass, and millwork, as well as FF&E sourcing, is highly desirable;
* Bachelor’s degree in Supply Chain Management, Business Administration, or a related field;
* Proven expertise in negotiation, contracting, PO issuance, and vendor performance management;
* Proficiency in Excel and major e-procurement and ERP platforms (e.g., SAP);
* Fluency in English;
* Positive and flexible attitude, with strong teamwork and problem-solving skills.

Nice to have: knowledge of Italian will be considered a plus.

*Pardgroup is an equal opportunity employer.*

ENABLE your future through light.


Excelitas is a global technology leader with more than 7,500 employees, focused on delivering market-driven solutions to fulfill the illumination, optical, detection and imaging needs of OEMs and end-users across the biomedical, semiconductor, industrial, consumer products, scientific, security, defense and aerospace sectors.


ENGAGE with us today and make your contribution to the future! Join the team that leading technology companies turn to for cutting-edge photonic innovation. At Excelitas Technologies you are how we EXCEL.


Excelitas is a global technology leader with more than 7,500 employees, focused on delivering market-driven solutions to fulfill the illumination, optical, detection and imaging needs of OEMs and end-users across the biomedical, semiconductor, industrial, consumer products, scientific, security, defense and aerospace sectors.


ENGAGE with us today and make your contribution to the future! Join the team that leading technology companies turn to for cutting-edge photonic innovation. At Excelitas Technologies you are how we EXCEL.


Our facility in Billerica, Massachusetts is located in the metropolitan Boston area and specializes in the design and manufacturing of advanced photonics products based on MEMS and other micro-scale optical devices. Our unique technology enables the highest system performance in the most compact and cost-effective formats in a variety of applications.


This site's Optical Coherence Tomography (OCT) products are laser-based imaging tools that have transformed ophthalmic care and made notable impacts on patients in cardiology, dermatology, oncology, gastroenterology, and other medical specialties.


**Senior Buyer**
We are presently seeking a Sr. Buyer in our Billerica site. This position is responsible for the procurement of services, equipment and materials required to support daily operations of the company. Negotiates and procures inventory and non inventory goods and services at lowest acquisition cost consistent with quality limits of Excelitas Technologies Corporation.


**Main Responsibilities**

* Solicits bids, analyzes quotations against specifications and selects suppliers with the proper capabilities to support goods and services;
* Partner with work cells to procure services and materials;
* Provide analyses and recommendations to support purchasing and scheduling decisions;
* Process purchase requisitions and create purchase orders;
* Maintain contract files, purchase order files and appropriate tracking system;
* Stay current with market requirements, resources, pricing and trends;
* Negotiates purchases at the lowest acquisition cost;
* Effectively communicate with internal customers and suppliers;
* Negotiate terms and conditions with suppliers;
* Performs other related duties of comparable complexity as directed.

**Requirements**

* Requires a high school education plus specialized courses;
* 5-7 years experience in purchase expediting, material or inventory control;
* Must be capable of reading blueprints and schematics;
* Effectively communicates with and engages all levels of the organization verbally and in writing;

**Compensation**

* Salary Range - $110,000 - $145,000 (Depending on Experience

