* The ability to develop, lead, motivate, and continuously improve within a global sourcing team.
* Proficiency of establishing relationships with key business and technology partners that assure alignment and successful outcomes
* Timely identification and efficient execution of key supplier projects and continuous improvement initiatives
* Competency in positioning team to implement a supply base that can fully support the successful launch of new products
* Identification and implementation of new supplier management elements to enhance the Global Procurement organization
* The capacity to leverage key suppliers to support Entegris growth and profitability goals



**Requirements:**




* BS or MS in engineering, supply chain or related;
* The ability to understand total cost models;
* A leader with a strong technical background in part fabrication with the ability to effectively motivate teams to achieve collective success;
* An astute capability to recognize the needs and motivations of individuals, and the capability to develop and nurture a wide array of internal and external relationships;
* The capability to quickly understand complex engagements, identify creative business solutions, and drive successful interactions with outside partners;
* A dedicated technology inclination for learning, collaborating, and continuous improvement;
* Demonstrated negotiating skills, effective communication capabilities, and the ability to persuade suppliers to efficiently support the long term, profitable growth of Entegris;
* Strong plastic fabrication fundamentals, with the ability to apply his/her knowledge to current and emerging semiconductor manufacturing needs.

